menu "Sirens and outputs (outputs_service)"

    config ALARM_OUTPUTS
        bool "Wired outputs and 433 MHz sirens"
        default y
        help
            The panel's own sirens and outputs (docs/features/16): a siren, a strobe, the smoke
            detectors' power or an "armed" light on a wired terminal through a relay or MOSFET
            module, and the cheap one-way 433 MHz sirens, which the panel transmits to (a
            CC1101, or a transmitter module set with `rf txpin`). Nothing is driven until an
            output is configured (`out` on the console, or Installer > Sirens and outputs), and
            a terminal an output takes is no longer offered to the wired zones.

endmenu
